      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68219,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68220,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>Low-grade papillary adenocarcinoma of the thymus is localized in the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T11:38:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68221,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients may be asymptomatic {30959362; 20859731; 18611939; 9669349} or have cough, chest pain, and dyspnoea {29339175; 9669349}. High serum levels of CEA may occur {30959362}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Imaging reveals well-circumscribed, partially cystic or solid lesions in the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum, as well as tumours with invasion into the lung and intrathoracic dissemination {9669349; 20859731; 30959362}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T11:38:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68222,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary adenocarcinoma represents 3% in a series of 65&nbsp;thymic carcinomas {22706865}. The mean age of presentation was 52&nbsp;years, with no sex predilection {18611939}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68223,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A subset of papillary adenocarcinomas appear to arise from type&nbsp;A or AB thymoma or from multilocular thymic cysts {9669349; 21677542; 22706865; 20549461}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68224,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68225,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours may be completely or partially encapsulated and show cystic and solid areas. In multilocular cysts they may form nodular protrusions {22706865}. The mean size is 65 mm {18611939}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-03T11:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68226,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "<p>Tubulopapillary structures are lined by cuboidal or polygonal cells with mildly atypical round to oval nuclei, small distinct nucleoli, and eosinophilic or clear cytoplasm. Nuclei may show grooves and irregularities; mitotic figures can be present {22706865}. Fibrovascular cores are present in some papillae. Psammoma bodies and coagulative necrosis can be present. Discernible type&nbsp;A or AB thymoma elements may be found within a main tumour.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The tumour shows positivity for cytokeratins (including CK8 and CK7), EMA, BerEP4, and vimentin; variable and focal positivity for CD5, CEA, calretinin, CD15, and KIT (CD117) {9669349; 16039252; 29339175}; and negativity for CK20, CDX2, thyroglobulin, TTF1, calcitonin, FOXN1, p63, p40, CD20, and PAX8 {29339175; 20859731; 18611939}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Thymic carcinomas with papillary features and high-grade atypia are classified as thymic adenocarcinomas NOS instead. Ectopic or metastatic thyroid carcinoma, mesothelioma, mediastinal extension of papillary adenocarcinoma of the lung, and metastasis from other organs must be excluded. Of note, unlike in squamous or squamous-related carcinomas, CD5 expression in adenocarcinomas is not indicative of a thymic origin {19276352}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T10:34:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68227,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not available</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68228,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68229,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A primary thymic low-grade adenocarcinoma with areas of tubulopapillary growth</li>\r\n<li>Tubulopapillary structures lined by cuboidal or polygonal cells</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Immunostains to exclude papillary neoplasms of the thyroid, pleura, lung, and extrathoracic sites</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-22T16:25:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68230,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "<p>Low-grade papillary adenocarcinomas should be staged according to the TNM system [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]] {25396314} and, optionally, the Masaoka&ndash;Koga system {21847052}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T10:34:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68231,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 238,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About 50% of cases recur, but tumour-related death is uncommon {9669349; 18611939; 29339175}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:05:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]